    "text": "New robot from Chula to help in battle against Covid-19\nTech\nNew robot from Chula to help in battle against Covid-19\nWEDNESDAY, APRIL 08, 2020\nสลับเป็นเสียงผู้ชาย\nPlay\nLoading...\nChulalongkorn University’s Faculty of Engineering launched “CU-RoboCovid” on Wednesday (April 8) to help doctors and nurses who are in the frontline of the battle against Covid-19.\nThe new robot was created to help doctors reduce their risk of infection, ease their workload and boost the efficiency of caretakers.\nThe robot was developed in cooperation with Mi Workspace, HG Robotics and Obodroid.\nThe group had previously created the “Pinto” and “Ninja” robots to help in the battle against the virus.\nThe Pinto robot is used to deliver food or medical supplies, while Ninja is connected to monitors that can send information about the patient’s blood pressure, pulse, temperature etc directly to the doctor.\nThe developers aim to provide 103 Pinto robots to medical personnel to mark the Chulalongkorn University Alumni Association’s 103rd anniversary this year. Presently, 20 such robots are working at Chulalongkorn, Siriraj and Vachira Phuket hospitals.\nRelated\nTourism sector advised to embrace digital technology\nSeptember 08, 2022\nApple's new satellite service for iPhone 14 'a big deal'\nSeptember 08, 2022\nStudy reveals 5 Key Trends for continued surge in time spent on mobile devices\nSeptember 07, 2022\nTAGS\nsocial\nTech\nChula\nrobot\nMOST VIEWED\n1.\nJapan Foreign Minister urges Russia to free detained reporter\n2.\nJapan government  remains cautious on declaring end to deflation\n3.\nRussian-Thai Investment Forum Closes with New Business Pact and $4.5bn Project Potential\n4.\nBangkok and central Thailand face heavy rain as thundershowers continue\n5.\nRussian and Thai Business Leaders Call for Pivot to Joint Ventures and Tech Partnerships\n©\n2026\nAll rights reserved.,\nThe Nation\nPrivacy Policy"
